{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788276056,"nonce":"S4NdvFj6cCI2cX9ONh9j/tkxzVE=","message":"BENCH PASS DONE — STAYING OPEN ON TWO BULLETS. Assembly `25b65ff`, 2026-09-01.\nRecord: `accept/runs/s15-20260901/`.\n\n\n- **`site-survey`'s verdict is the game's own sentence.** Wall on the\n  interaction cell → *\"Interaction spot is blocked by wooden wall.\"*, and\n  `dev:spawn-thing` with the same arguments returned the SAME string verbatim.\n  One routine, two callers — the core of this issue's design, confirmed.\n- **Corner↔centre, exactly.** `pos [135,145]` → footprint corner `[134,145]`.\n  And the round-trip that pins it: candidate `at [124,125] 3x2 rot North pos\n  [125,125]`, spawned at its own `pos`, read back `rect [124,125,3,2]`. The\n  approved box and the occupied rect are the same box. That is the failure this\n  issue was filed on, closed.\n- **The even-axis rotation shift.** `pos [125,125] rot South` for a 3x2 def →\n  footprint corner `[124,124]`, i.e. `AdjustForRotation`'s z shift applied only\n  to the even axis. Two positions computed from it (`[125,127]` North and\n  `[125,125]` South) were confirmed to share interaction cell `[125,126]`, with\n  footprints that touch neither it nor each other — arithmetic the old code\n  could not express.\n- **The widget gate, and it refuses BEFORE searching.**\n  `find-rect --def HiTechResearchBench` → `examined: 0, gate_calls: 0`,\n  `selectable: {ok:false, source:\"Designator_Build.Visible\", clause:\"research\",\n  detail:\"HiTechResearchBench needs research 'MicroelectronicsBasics'\"}`. That\n  is `1adc737` amendment #1's warning (\"`build` will cheerfully blueprint\n  unresearched buildings — a god-hand that looks correct\") closed, with the\n  clause as a token rather than a parsed sentence, through `WorldSafe.Finished`.\n- **The margin tier is real.** 3x2 footprint → 9x8 surveyed rect\n  (`margin: 3, margin_default: 3`), 65 cells, 60 standable, `notable: 5 /\n  listed: 5 / more: 0`, plus reachability of the interaction cell from the first\n  free colonist. Evan's \"2-3x bigger than whatever they're building\",\n  delivered, with the ASCII crop riding in the same result.\n- **The interaction-spot OVERLAP rule.** Two benches wanting `[125,126]` →\n  *\"Interaction spot overlaps with the interaction spot of wooden simple\n  research bench.\"*, `tiers.interaction[0].reason: \"interaction-overlap\"`,\n  blocker naming the other bench.\n- **The REVERSE rule too**, which is not in this issue's text:\n  `NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells` → *\"Simple research bench would block simple\n  research bench's interaction spot.\"*\n- **`find-rect {w,h}` untouched** — `923800b` is 340 insertions, ZERO deletions\n  in `SpatialVerbs.cs`. Stronger than the comparison run the Acceptance asked\n  for.\n- `gate = \"site-gate/1\"` — the routine carries a versioned identity, matching\n  the alphabet-id convention.\n\n\n**1. The tolerated chair is not LISTED.** The Acceptance says: *\"A chair on the\ninteraction cell: `verdict.ok:true`, the chair listed under `tiers.interaction`\nas tolerated.\"* The verdict half is proven. The listing half is not — with a\n`DiningChair` on the cell the tier reports:\n\n    {at: [130,134], role: \"interaction\", ok: true, reason: null,\n     blocker: null, standable: true}\n\nNo occupant named. So an agent cannot distinguish \"a chair is there, which is\nfine\" from \"the cell is empty\", and the difference is load-bearing: that chair\nis precisely what the NEXT bench's `PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap`\nwill trip on. `blocker` is the wrong field for it (nothing is blocking); the\ncell wants an `occupants` or `tolerated` list. Small, and it is a shape gap\nrather than a behaviour bug.\n\n**2. \"the verdict is IDENTICAL to what `build` later returns\" is untestable\ntoday.** `build` and `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` are session B. Half the\npair is proven (survey ≡ `dev:spawn-thing`'s current refusal); the other half\narrives with B, and B's acceptance should assert it rather than re-deriving it.\n\n**Also unexercised, for want of ground rather than code:** the rotation search\nnever had to rotate. On open desert `def.defaultPlacingRot` fit everywhere, so\nall 8 candidates came back `rot: North` and `refusals: []`. The corridor case —\n*\"a corridor two cells deep with rock either side takes the 5x2 bench facing\neast and nothing facing north\"* — needs a staged fixture, and the only 5x2 def\nto hand is research-gated on a fresh map. `rot_order: [\"North\",\"East\",\"South\",\n\"West\"]` is published and correct; that the search actually FALLS THROUGH to\nEast is still unproven.","files":null}]}